     "Warm requests the purged pages anonymously, then every AVIF width of the images in each page's first row. Amended by feature 012 (012 research R-07): production runs the same provider with page purge on (`Edge:PurgePages = true`, `Edge:SiteBaseUrl = https://port.zacal.me`, and a token limited to Zone > Cache Purge on `zacal.me`); its mode label stays `dev-zone` (012 decisions #16). Warm requests go through Cloudflare, so they carry the origin secret and pass the guard (D-03). A Cloudflare Cache Rule on `port.zacal.me` makes HTML eligible for caching and respects the origin's `s-maxage=86400`; it bypasses the cache when the request carries the `__Host-gallery` cookie and for every path under `/admin`, `/signin-oidc`, `/signout-callback-oidc` and `/ui`.\n",
